.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLAB 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm klab
.Nd build golden images of five distributions, run blue and green sites from them, and test ZFS across them
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Cm menu
.Nm
.Cm golden | golden-ztest | golden-desktop | golden-xfce | golden-kde | golden-db
.Op Ar distro ... | Cm all
.Nm
.Cm deploy | promote | destroy
.Ar site
.Nm
.Cm rollback | build-all | status
.Nm
.Cm test
.Op Fl -quick | -full
.Op Fl -distro Ar list
.Nm
.Cm verify
.Op Ar distro | Cm all
.Nm
.Cm results
.Op Ar run-id
.Nm
.Cm kubernetes
.Op Fl -workers Ar n
.Op Ar distro
.Nm
.Cm run-playbook Ar script
.Nm
.Cm fetch-rhel-image
.Op Fl -output Ar path
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
builds a golden image of each of CentOS, Rocky, Fedora, Debian and Ubuntu
\(em a cloud image made into a ZFS volume, set up, validated, shut down
and snapshotted \(em and makes machines from them as instant clones.
There are several lineages:
.Bl -tag -width "golden-desktop" -compact
.It Cm golden
The regular image, ZFS included, kept small.
.It Cm golden-ztest
With the OpenZFS test suite, its dependencies and loopback devices, for
.Cm test .
.It Cm golden-desktop , golden-xfce , golden-kde
GNOME, Xfce or KDE Plasma desktops, without ZFS in the guest.
.It Cm golden-db
PostgreSQL with a generated dataset, to clone one per developer.
.El
.Pp
A golden that exists and validated is kept, so building again takes
seconds; one whose last validation failed is rebuilt.
The blue site is the running set of machines and green the next;
.Cm promote
makes green the new blue after snapshotting blue, and
.Cm rollback
returns blue to that snapshot.
.Pp
It runs itself under
.Xr sudo 8 .
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm golden Oo Ar distro ... | Cm all Oc
And the other lineages, as above.
.It Cm deploy Cm blue | green
Clone the goldens into that site.
.It Cm promote Cm green
Green becomes blue.
.It Cm rollback
Blue back to its snapshot from before the last promotion.
.It Cm build-all
Every golden, then both sites, in one run; a second run while one is
going is refused.
.It Cm test Oo Fl -quick | Fl -full Oc Op Fl -distro Ar list
The OpenZFS test suite on the ztest goldens' clones.
.It Cm verify Op Ar distro | Cm all
Boot each golden's clone and check it.
.It Cm status
The goldens, the sites, the last results and the logs.
.It Cm results Op Ar run-id
A run's matrix of passes and failures.
.It Cm kubernetes Oo Fl -workers Ar n Oc Op Ar distro
A cluster by
.Xr kube-cluster 8 ;
three workers by default.
.It Cm run-playbook Ar script
Run a script on the blue site's machines.
.It Cm destroy Cm blue | green | all | goldens
Remove a site, both, or the goldens.
.It Cm fetch-rhel-image
Download the RHEL guest image with saved Red Hat credentials.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -zfs-version Ar v , Fl -zfs-git Ar repo@branch , Fl -zfs-tarball Ar path
Build ZFS into the goldens from a release, a git branch or a tarball.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print usage and exit 0.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev KLAB_DB_SCALE
The size of
.Cm golden-db Ns 's
dataset: 200 is about 3 GB, 3400 about 500 GB.
.It Ev KLAB_ZFS_DEV
1 puts the test suite into the image;
.Cm golden-ztest
sets it.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /root/klab/
Logs and results:
.Pa klab.log ,
.Pa goldens/ Ns Ar distro Ns Pa -latest.log
with each golden's validation, and one directory per test run.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when done; 1 on a failure, named.
